ds.com/review/show/5721679390">July 28, 2023</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">The mischievous, “carefree” character who is fighting serious internal demons is my favoriteeeeee kind of love interest.<br /><br /><b>MAIN CHARACTER NAMES AND AGES</b><br />Keira Sartin (?) <b>|</b> Alexi Skolov (~24)<br /><br /><b>FEATURES</b><br />∘ sci-fi mafia romance<br />∘ omegaverse<br />∘ fated mates<br />∘ hulk-like alter ego<br />∘ dangerous to everyone but her / only <i>she</i> can calm him<br /><br /><b>REVIEW</b><br />Keira and Alexi are probably my favorite couple of the series. They’ve not had it easy in their respective lives, but with the other’s help, they set each other free (literally in Kiera’s case, figuratively in Alexi’s).<br /><br />I appreciated that Keira was realistically afraid of Alexi’s berserketh alter ego at first. She stops fearing it when she realizes he’d never hurt her, and for most of the novel, Alexi is more fearful of it than she is. His inner monologue about how much of a monster was did get repetitive (and significantly lengthened the novel), but otherwise, the pacing was great.<br /><br />We finally get some answers—and new questions—to the overarching plot to the series. I love a conspiracy, and there’s plenty to go around in this universe.<br /><br />With each entry I read, I fall a little more in love with the series. <br /><br /><b>OW/OM DRAMA</b> none<br /><b>CHEATING</b> none<br /><b>THIRD ACT BREAKUP</b> no<br /><b>ENDING</b> HEA — epilogue set in near future<br /><br /><b>POV</b> dual / third person<br /><b>SPICE LEVEL</b> 4 / 5<br /><b>RATING</b> 4.5 / 5<br /><br /><br /><br /><i>For those who DNFed and want answers…</i><br /><br /><b>SPOILERS</b><br /><br /><b>Twin Status</b><br /><input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="139b0390-e769-4169-ae12-ef2592e27d94" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="139b0390-e769-4169-ae12-ef2592e27d94">As we know, the Skolov siblings have been searching for their missing twin siblings. They discover that the identity of their younger brother is Maddox, Baro’s “son” and heir. He used someone else’s blood for the DNA test so that he could retain his position as the Sartin heir to overthrow the evil Baro.<br /><br />Their sister’s location/identity has no updates.</label> <br /><br /><b>Who is Rose?</b><br /><input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="71fe9b21-c4a4-4f4b-87ab-e7bf2fe2d39d" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="71fe9b21-c4a4-4f4b-87ab-e7bf2fe2d39d">Whenever Alexi starts to lose control and the berserketh takes over, he sees someone named Rose.<br /><br />She was a pleasure omega who propositioned Alexi after his brutal kidnapping and torture. She touches him to get his attention, and he loses control and slashes her brutally. He had to be stunned, but Rose survived. She has since been financially compensated and has moved on. She doesn’t appear in the story, although Alexi harbors severe guilt over this.</label><br /><br /><b>Baro’s Traitor</b><br /><input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="3d4b81a5-b6cc-4883-ad9d-2af2eaf3125f" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="3d4b81a5-b6cc-4883-ad9d-2af2eaf3125f">The individual who has been setting Baro up and snitching to the Brotherhood is Dugar Sartin, Keira’s father and Baro’s brother. He was resentful that the Sartin heir isn’t his son, Cole, and instead is Baro’s son (who isn’t actually his son). <br /><br />He has been trying for years to overthrow Baro, and almost succeeds, if it weren’t for those meddling kids.</label><br /><br /><b>The Identity of the Series Antagonist</b><br /><input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="4d85c7cd-217d-40bd-9cc0-abd06d853013" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="4d85c7cd-217d-40bd-9cc0-abd06d853013">This was a significant entry in the series, as we discover the identity of the culprit who stole the twins and has continuously tried to harm the Skolovs. <br /><br />He was born Darvish Sartin (a distant relative of Keira) to an omega of the Sartin line. She was expected to make a good match, but was “seduced by an off-planet Alpha who made no offer to procure her and claim her as his prime omega, even once her breeding state became known.”<br /><br />At birth, he was pronounced “defective” because he was missing a horn. For this reason, his mother and he were exiled by Baro’s father. <br /><br />Darvish’s father is none other than Burian Skolov (father of the Skolov siblings), meaning that Darvish is their [the protagonists of this series] half-brother. <br /><br /><s>I had to reread this information at least three times because I thought Darvish was Dugar (Keira’s father), and I was like no way did they just make this main couple incestuous. Upon reread, that is not the case. Because while Keira and Alexi may both be related to Darvish, they are NOT related to each other.</s></label></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/145247010?shelf=alien" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">alien</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/145247010?shelf=fated-mates" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">fated-mates</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/145247010?shelf=monster" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">monster</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">23 likes</span></button></div><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">2 comments</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19.1708204,11.4980616 L19.118034,11.6036344 L19.1708204,11.7092072 C19.4523479,12.2722622 19.4523479,12.9350066 19.1708204,13.4980616 L19.118034,13.6036344 L19.1708204,13.7092072 C19.4523479,14.2722622 19.4523479,14.9350066 19.1708204,15.4980616 L19,15.8397024 L19,16.1036344 C19,16.7361314 18.6701344,17.3185188 18.1373501,17.6453922 L17.9472136,17.7480616 C17.4795438,17.9818965 16.9638538,18.1036344 16.440983,18.1036