d="path_RatingStar_undefined0small" d="M24 9.63469C24 9.35683 23.7747 9.13158 23.4969 9.13158H15.0892L12.477 1.34327C12.4269 1.19375 12.3095 1.0764 12.16 1.02625C11.8966 0.937894 11.6114 1.07983 11.523 1.34327L8.91088 9.13158H0.503157C0.33975 9.13158 0.186521 9.21094 0.0922364 9.3444C-0.0680877 9.57134 -0.0140806 9.88529 0.212865 10.0456L7.00408 14.8432L4.40172 22.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined0small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined0small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4615289015">March 26, 2022</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted"><b><s>The Incredible Hulk</s> Alexi Meets Keira</b><br /><br />This is the third in the author's dystopian Mafia Omegaverse; since each entry features one Skolov sibling, we're now on brother three: the most physically powerful and also the most damaged. Severely affected by cruel scientific experiments that left him with even greater-than-usual Alpha strength and an inability to control murderous rages, Alexi comes to Keira's uncle's compound to search for his missing little brother, but his immediate attraction to his fated mate throws him momentarily off-track. Can his "Starlight" tame the monster within him? Note: Although the MC meet for the first time here, so many characters, plot points, and one overarching mystery (the Skolovs' search for their youngest siblings, missing since infancy) continue from previous books that I think it's best to read the books in order. <br /><br />As with the other entries, I really liked this, particularly four aspects. First, the worldbuilding is hauntingly visceral (the descriptions of the planet's pleasure district and the Sartin estate evoke the apocalyptic underworld hellishness of <i>Metropolis</i>, <i>Strange Days</i>, and <i>Blade Runner</i> combined). Second, the plot twists were ones I didn't see coming and, thus, genuine surprises. Third, Ms. Aimes introduces disability into what is usually a very abled genre. And, finally, the MC was extremely sympathetic with competing motivations that create organic conflict (while Alexi wants nothing more than to rescue Keira from her abusive uncle, she wants to stay in order to protect the other Omegas). I really liked that the usual Omegaverse insta-love was deepened by a connection that went beyond the sexual: both are "damaged" (Keira is considered "defective" because she's giftless and barren); therefore, each understands the pain and humiliation the other feels. While this takes the "good girl/bad boy" trope to the nth degree, I didn't mind it here because Keira actively participates in the narrative; her intelligence and inner strength apparent throughout (it's interesting that her <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="566fa9e6-8161-4a66-864a-22f95a8b75fa" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="566fa9e6-8161-4a66-864a-22f95a8b75fa">gift turns out to be one that may or not be magical</label>). I spent the entire book hoping they'd get their HEA and there's no higher praise for a book in this genre than that.<br /><br />I do have some quibbles. This didn't need to be as long as it was (editing Alexi's repetitive "I'm a monster" dialogue would have cut off a good chunk); there were a few too many double bluffs and climaxes (plot, not sexual) towards the end to be remotely plausible; and I would have liked to have seen Keira interact with <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="e35e4712-d799-4ecd-9155-833db7741717" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="e35e4712-d799-4ecd-9155-833db7741717">her sisters-in-law</label>. But Ms. Aimes has created such a warm, vibrant, close-knit family in the Skolovs that these are minor criticisms.<br /><br />4 1/2 stars. Damien is up next. Side Notes: I hope we see the female underground railroad rescue pilot again and "scent mufflers" have new meaning in the Age of COVID.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/98512744?shelf=consenusal" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">consenusal</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/98512744?shelf=descriptive" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">descriptive</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/98512744?shelf=good-girl-bad-boy" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">good-girl-bad-boy</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span> <div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium" aria-label="Show all items in the list"><span class="Button__labelItem">...more</span></button></div></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Bu