https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4601520080">March 11, 2022</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">Mmmm Alexi, you growly hunk of deliciousness...<br />If I were to choose a book boyfriend from Alison Aimes' Dark Mafia Omegaverse, it would be Alexi Skolov... and maybe Damien... but definitely Alexi. Well, I have to wait a while for Damien's book, but Alexi's story was so satisfying. <br /><br />Alison Aimes has crafted another heart pounding adventure with all the feels. Broken Heir pivots us to another corner of Anarcheim - the Alphaverse galaxy. This time to the seedy Sartin crime family where our female main character, Keira Sartin, has lived her life practically squashed under sticky Sartin alpha boots. My heart goes out to Keira and all she has endured but the abuse forged a soul of steel and a unique omega power. I loved this aspect of the story... her power isn't showy, but strong all the same. <br /><br />Alexi also endured soul-breaking abuse at the hands of abductors when he was young. While these scenes may trigger someone with a history of abuse, the author does a good job at keeping the story moving through the back-flashes and (thankfully) does not get graphic with those scenes. They are not gratuitous and the history is necessary as Alexi's present "condition" is a result of his captivity, which plays a very big role in the story.<br /><br />I love Keira and Alexi. Obviously, there is danger and conflict around every corner and a sense of precariousness in their time together. Like all Alison Aimes stories, it moves at a fast pace, but Keira and Alexi manage to carve out some steamy love times. I love a dirty talker and Alexi is just that. In fact, the book starts right off with a teaser scene to get you salivating. Luckily, you don't have to wait long for the main course. <br /><br />Broken Heir also brings home one long-lost Skolov sibling. I don't want to spoil the story, but it was totally satisfying. I cannot wait to find out where the other twin has been hiding. Something tells me they are as kick-@$$ as their siblings.<br /><br />Damien's story is up next and, based on the bonus epilogue provided, it is going to be yummy!<br /><br />By the way, I received an advanced reader copy in exchange for my honest review.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">3 likes</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19.1708204,11.4980616 L19.118034,11.6036344 L19.1708204,11.7092072 C19.4523479,12.2722622 19.4523479,12.9350066 19.1708204,13.4980616 L19.118034,13.6036344 L19.1708204,13.7092072 C19.4523479,14.2722622 19.4523479,14.9350066 19.1708204,15.4980616 L19,15.8397024 L19,16.1036344 C19,16.7361314 18.6701344,17.3185188 18.1373501,17.6453922 L17.9472136,17.7480616 C17.4795438,17.9818965 16.9638538,18.1036344 16.440983,18.1036344 L9.668341